From 9b948caea019524b28d20f6c55fa5843a6e8e751 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dmitry Minkovsky <dminkovsky@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 12:00:18 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Follow a queue reorder through the lane's rows, not a version

The Mac and Android queues read the context lane as the upcoming list: each
row held in place keeps its window read, and a drop shows until the lane's
rows draw the moved row where it was dropped. With nothing waiting on them,
the queue row's two versions, their bumps, the old offset windows and the
bridge fields that carried them go; a reorder answers whether it moved.

